Article 14
Special protection for children is provided to;
(1)
a. Children in emergency situations;
b. Children in contact with the law;
c. Children from minority and isolated groups;
d. Children who are exploited economically and/or sexually;
e. Children who are victims of narcotics abuse, alcohol, psychotropic substances, and other addictive substances;
f. Children who are victims of pornography;
g. Children with HIV/AIDS;
h. Children who are victims of kidnapping, sale, and/or trafficking;
i. Children who are victims of physical and/or psychological violence;
j. Children who are victims of sexual crimes;
k. Children who are victims of terrorist networks;
l. Children with Disabilities;
m. Children who are victims of maltreatment and neglect;
n. Children with deviant social behavior; and
o. Children who are victims of stigmatization from labeling related to the condition of their Parents.
(2) Regional governments in implementing the handling as referred to in paragraph (1) in accordance with the provisions of the Laws and Regulations.

Article 3
The objectives of the protection of women and children from acts of violence are to:
a. prevent violence against women and children, including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;
d. provide services and empowerment to women and children who are victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
e. facilitate and conduct mediation of domestic disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household; and
f. facilitate the restoration of the rights, dignity, and personal value of victims.

Article 13
(1) The provisions regarding the prevention of and services for acts of violence against women as referred to in Article 7 up to Article 12 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the protection of children from acts of violence;
(2) In addition to carrying out the prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), it shall also be carried out by increasing the capacity of families in child protection and child-rearing skills.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
Protection of Women and Children from Acts of Violence, is implemented based on the principles of:
a. respect and fulfillment of the rights of Victims of Acts of Violence;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. non-discrimination;
d. the best interests of Victims of acts of violence; and
e. The principle of the right to life, survival and development,

Article 12
(1) The protection of children who are victims of acts of violence as referred to in article 5 letter a shall be the responsibility of the Regional Government. (2) The protection of child victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by means of: a. formulating policies for prevention, reduction of vulnerable risks, handling of victims and child data and information systems; b. providing maintenance, care, and social rehabilitation for neglected children, both within institutions and outside institutions;
c. providing shelters, maintenance and care for neglected children; and d. providing special protection to children.

REGENT OF NORTH LAMPUNG
REGIONAL REGULATION OF NORTH LAMPUNG REGENCY
NUMBER 1 YEAR 2017
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
FROM ACTS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF ALMIGHTY GOD
REGENT OF NORTH LAMPUNG,
Considering : a. that women and children have the right to obtain a sense of security and freedom from all forms of torture or treatment that degrades human dignity, therefore they need to obtain optimal legal protection;
b. that based on Article 9 paragraph (3) and paragraph (4), as well as Article 12 paragraph (2) letter b of Law Number 23 Year 2014 concerning Regional Government, it is stated that women's empowerment and child protection are mandatory governmental affairs not related to basic services of the government and are the responsibility of the North Lampung Regency government;
c. that based on the considerations in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Women's Empowerment and Protection of Children from Acts of Violence
