Article 16
(1) The Regional Government in conducting cooperation and coordination regarding the Protection of Women and Children from acts of violence, shall establish a Forum for the Care of Women and Children from Acts of Violence (FP2ATK);
(2) The membership of FP2ATK consists of elements of:
a. regional government;
b. vertical agencies;
c. educational institutions;
d. health institutions;
e. social institutions;
f. labor institutions; and
g. community organizations that care about the protection of women and children from acts of violence.
(3) The Organizational Structure of FP2ATK as referred to in paragraph (2) consists of:
a. policy formulation working group;
b. socialization working group;
c. service working group; and
d. data, information, monitoring and evaluation working group.
(4) The establishment and term of office of FP2ATK members as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be stipulated by a Decree of the Regent.

Article 17
FP2ATK has the duties:
a. to provide input in the formulation of policies;
b. to coordinate with Regional Apparatus Organizations and other social institutions;
c. to disseminate laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
d. to collect and develop data and information related to the protection of women and children from acts of violence;
e. to conduct review, monitoring, evaluation and supervision of the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence; and
f. to provide reports, suggestions, input and considerations to the Regent.

Article 13
(1) The provisions regarding the prevention of and services for acts of violence against women as referred to in Article 7 up to Article 12 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the protection of children from acts of violence;
(2) In addition to carrying out the prevention as referred to in paragraph (1), it shall also be carried out by increasing the capacity of families in child protection and child-rearing skills.

