(1) The Regent coordinates the protection of women and children from acts of violence with: a. the government;
b. other regency/regional governments;
c. vertical agencies;
d. educational institutions; and
e. community institutions.
(2) Coordination as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. religious affairs;
b. health affairs;
b. education affairs;
c. social affairs;
d. legal affairs;
e. labor affairs; and £. other affairs.

