Article 7
(1) The Regional Government carries out prevention as referred to in Article 6 letter a by means of:
  a. disseminating laws and regulations;
  b. providing counseling/guidance;
  c. providing education on the dangers of domestic violence;
  d. conducting seminars/workshops or the like;
  e. establishing work networks in efforts to prevent violence;
  f. conducting coordination, integration, and synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
  g. establishing a violence prevention system, mapping locations or areas prone to violence; and
  h. increasing public awareness to behave in accordance with religious norms and customs.
(2) In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) must be implemented by:
  a. religious institutions;
  b. family and/or closest relatives;
  c. customary leaders;
  d. customary institutions;
  e. the community;
  f. educational institutions;
  g. health institutions;
  h. social community institutions; and
  i. the business sector and other institutions.

