c. providing shelters, maintenance and care for neglected children; and d. providing special protection to children.

Article 21
(1) In certain circumstances, the Regional Government may conduct cooperation regarding women and children from acts of violence with:
a. other regional governments;
b. the police;
b. advocates;
c. health workers;
d. social workers;
e. volunteer companions;
f. spiritual counselors;
g. other law enforcers, to assist victims in the court trial process;
h. the national commission on anti-violence against women;
i. the Indonesian Child Protection Commission or Child Protection Institution; and/or
j. certain parties desired for the benefit of the victim.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) may be in the form of:
a. socialization;
b. provision of legal aid;
c. health services;
d. victim assistance;
e. counseling;
f. social rehabilitation;
g. spiritual guidance; and/or
h. repatriation and social reintegration.

Article 6
Every person who hears, sees, or knows of the occurrence of violence as referred to in Article 5 is obligated to make efforts to:
a. prevent the continuation of criminal acts;
b. provide protection to victims of acts of violence;
c. provide emergency assistance; and/or
d. [text illegible in source].

