Article 19
Further provisions regarding the mechanism and working procedures of FP2ATK shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 20
(1) The Regional Government, in the context of services for victims of acts of violence, shall establish P2TP2A.
(2) P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall have the duties of:

a. providing services, including:
1. receiving complaints/reports of violence against women and/or children, consultation, and counseling;
2. receiving and sending case referrals from the Regency/City Regional Government or institutions established by the Regency/City Regional Government;
3. providing legal assistance;
4. health;
5. social rehabilitation;
6. legal services; and
7. return and social reintegration.

b. providing protection to victims of acts of violence, reporters and witnesses.
(3) The appointment of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by Regent Decree.
(4) Regional Apparatus shall conduct guidance for P2TP2A in carrying out duties as referred to in paragraph (2).

