(1) The protection of children who are victims of acts of violence as referred to in article 5 letter a shall be the responsibility of the Regional Government. (2) The protection of child victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented by means of: a. formulating policies for prevention, reduction of vulnerable risks, handling of victims and child data and information systems; b. providing maintenance, care, and social rehabilitation for neglected children, both within institutions and outside institutions;
c. providing shelters, maintenance and care for neglected children; and d. providing special protection to children.

Article 3
The objectives of the protection of women and children from acts of violence are to:
a. prevent violence against women and children, including trafficking in persons;
b. eliminate all forms of violence and exploitation against women and children;
c. protect and provide a sense of security for women and children;
d. provide services and empowerment to women and children who are victims of violence, reporters, and witnesses;
e. facilitate and conduct mediation of domestic disputes to realize the integrity of a harmonious and prosperous household; and
f. facilitate the restoration of the rights, dignity, and personal value of victims.

Article 19
Further provisions regarding the mechanism and working procedures of FP2ATK shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 20
(1) The Regional Government, in the context of services for victims of acts of violence, shall establish P2TP2A.
(2) P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall have the duties of:

a. providing services, including:
1. receiving complaints/reports of violence against women and/or children, consultation, and counseling;
2. receiving and sending case referrals from the Regency/City Regional Government or institutions established by the Regency/City Regional Government;
3. providing legal assistance;
4. health;
5. social rehabilitation;
6. legal services; and
7. return and social reintegration.

b. providing protection to victims of acts of violence, reporters and witnesses.
(3) The appointment of P2TP2A as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by Regent Decree.
(4) Regional Apparatus shall conduct guidance for P2TP2A in carrying out duties as referred to in paragraph (2).

